Now append task handling and AI into pawns.js replacing marker.

updateTask(sdt,gh):
```js
updateTask(sdt,gh) {
 const t=this.task; if(!t) return;
 if (t.type==='attack'||t.type==='hunt') { this.updateCombatTask(sdt); this.workAnim += sdt; return; }
 if (this.phase==='go') {
   const arrived=this.moveAlong(sdt);
   if (arrived) this.arrive();
   else check target validity (obj deleted etc.) → finish.
   return;
 }
 // work
 this.working=true; this.workAnim += sdt*(1+...);
 switch(t.type)...
}
```

Validity: if t.objId object dead → finish. If t.type eat item dead → finish. For haul item gone (another pawn took) → reselect? finish.

`arrive()`:
- switch:
  - build/chop/mine/etc → phase work; face object; working true. For cook/research.
  - harvest/plant → phase work.
  - haul: pick up: 
    ```js
    const item=t.item; if(!item||item.dead) return finish
    const qty=item.qty; const type=item.type; item.dead=true; item.reservedBy=null;
    this.carry={type,qty}; this.task={type:'haulDrop', itemType:type, qty, dest:null}; // release reservations for old; 
    const dest = w.stockpileSpot(...); if(!dest) finish
    this.task.dest=dest; this.phase='go'; this.path=w.pathToTile(this,dest.x,dest.y)||[]; if !path finish; if empty arrive
    ```
    But this.task replacement without release is fine (old task has no reservations now). Ensure no leftovers.
    Also haul: priority—if item still has reservedBy this.id, set null.
  - eat: 
    ```js
    const item=t.item; if dead finish; nutrition=ITEMS[item.type].food; w.removeItem(item,1); item.reservedBy=null;
    this.needs.food clamp + nutrition; addFloat;
    const seat=w.findFreeSeat(this); 
    this.task={type: seat?'eatSeat':'eat', item:null, seatId:...};
    if (seat) { seat.seatReservedBy=this.id; this.seatId=seat.id; path=w.pathToTile(this, seat.x,seat.y); phase go; if path==null -> stand eat work; else if empty phase work; else ... } 
    else { phase='work'; this.work=0; task.eatDuration=2.4; }
    ```
    For eatSeat when path arrives → seat position, face table, phase work. In arrive(), if t.type eatSeat → phase work, face table.
  - sleep: t.bed: position on bed tile; phase work; sleeping=true. Ground sleep: sleeping=true, phase work.
  - tend: phase work; face target.
  - move/wander/flee: finish.
  - haulDrop: drop item; addItem; this.carry=null; play; finish.
  - eatSeat: sit.
  - attack/hunt handled separately.

Take care: arrive called from beginTask when path empty for harvest (pawn standing crop), etc. For sleep path to bed tile (walkable, bed non-blocking). Good.

`tickBuild` etc. Each called with sdt:
- rate = workSpeed(skill)*sdt.
- progress store `this.work`.
- object work progress = this.work maybe. Renderer shows obj.work/obj.workNeeded; set obj.work = this.work for blueprint.
- On complete: completeBuild, gainSkill, finish.

For initial Aria task: beginTask set path; snapToWork sets phase work but doesn't set obj.work. In tickBuild, we increment this.work and set obj.work each tick. Good.

Chop: total obj.def.chopWork; obj.work = this.work for progress; complete: drop wood at nearby walkable; remove object; particles leaves; and mark designation cleared (removeObject does). Bram finishes. Render fallen tree? We remove immediately with leaf particle burst. Add a stump object? Nice: after chop, drop a "stump" object (non-blocking, not choppable) visually. Could add nature 'stump' in gen and place via world.placeNature; renderer draws. Let's do: world.placeNature('stump', x, y, {name:'Stump', blocks:false,...}) defined inline; objectsById registration; def minimal {name:'Stump', blocks:false, beauty:0, kind:'stump'}. Add def in NATURE? gen exports NATURE; pawns can import? Avoid cycle (pawns imported by gen, so pawns can't import gen). Define stump def inline. placeNature requires def with hp etc. Provide:
```js
w.placeNature('stump', obj.x,obj.y,{name:'Stump',blocks:false,hp:40,kind:'stump'})
```
Fine. Renderer draws type 'stump'.

Mine: total mineWork; drop stone/steel at nearest walkable; remove; set terrain gravel maybe; use w.setTerrain if terrain grass etc. Leave pit? Set terrain to gravel. Renderer.
- Mine designation maybe multiple tiles? rocks are 1 tile.

Harvest: duration 1.2; complete: yield = 4 * (agriculture?1.3:1), add grain at tile; cropPlanted=0; crops=0; release; particles leaf; gainSkill; finish. stats.
- Plant: 0.9; planted=1, growth=0.02; finish.

Cook: 5.5s; if meal count condition? Use 5 grain/meat. Completion: consume grain 5 else meat; if insufficient → finish. Add meals 3 at adjacent walkable; particles steam; stats.meals; gainSkill; release; finish. Also mood? no.
