```js
if (needs.food<10 || needs.rest<8) { this.finishTask(); return; }
```
only for colonists.

Tend: 2.8s; target loses bleed; hp+=; if medicine tech more; particles heal; play; finish.

Sleep: in update() we return early after tickSleep when sleeping; tickSleep is called from update. Sleep task phase work; rest increases in updateNeeds (already) then tickSleep checks wake. But updateNeeds called before tickSleep and adds rest. tickSleep: if rest>=95 or alarm → wake. Also hunger? Wake when fully rested. If it's morning and rest>70 maybe wake? RimWorld sleeps until rested. Keep. If world.raid active → wake handled by wake() in spawnRaid (sets awake and task=null). Need pawn position remains bed; fine.
