Now combat and AI. Need includes:
- updateCombat, reactToRaid, findRaiderInRange, tryAutoFire, tryShoot, updateCombatTask, approachCombat, updateRaider, updateAnimal, flee/heal.

Also `finishTask` drop carry logic: for delivered we call finishTask after setting carry null; fine.

`approachCombat(task, isHunt)` sets task, phase 'go', path empty, repathTimer 0. It should reserve hunt already. For drafted attack target raider.

`updateCombatTask(sdt)` described.

Drafted auto-fire while moving: updateCombat can call tryAutoFire if this.drafted; tryAutoFire only if no task or task phase work? Let's fire whenever target in range (even moving) but shooting while walking is okay. Fine. But if already attacking, updateCombatTask handles; avoid double shoot: skip if task.type === 'attack'.

Auto-defend:
`updateCombat(sdt, gh)`:
```js
if (this.dead || this.downed) return;
if (this.drafted) {
  if (!this.task || this.task.type !== 'attack') this.tryAutoFire();
  return;
}
if (this.world.raid?.active) {
  this.alarm = true;
  if (!this.task || !['attack','flee'].includes(this.task.type)) this.reactToRaid();
} else if (this.alarm) {
  this.alarm = false;
  if (this.task && (this.task.type==='attack'||this.task.type==='flee')) this.finishTask();
}
```
But updateCombat called before sleeping; sleeping colonists should wake if raid? spawnRaid calls wake for all. Later new raiders only via spawnRaid. Good.

reactToRaid: nearest raider; if none return. Determine if brave:
```js
const enemy = w.nearestRaider(...)
const d=dist
const ranged = weapon && WEAPONS[weapon]?.ranged;
const brave = ranged || this.hasTrait('brawler') || this.kind==='colonist' && this.skills.shooting>=5 || d<4
if (brave && (ranged || d<12)) beginTask attack
else flee inside
```
All except maybe Cleo (pistol) ranged → brave. Dax pistol. So all fight. Fine; animals flee.

But when attacker is far (e.g., 25 tiles away), brave ranged colonist might chase across map; that's okay during raid. They auto-engage. Elin in field, etc. Good.

Flee: find indoor tile (woodfloor) nearest (29,28). If unable, point away:
```js
const away = nearestWalkable(this.x + (this.x-enemy.x)*3, ...)
```
beginTask flee. When task flee finishes, reactToRaid would assign again if still raiders; okay. Could loop, fine.

`findRaiderInRange(range)` uses world.raid attackers.

`tryShoot(target)`:
```js
const wep=WEAPONS[this.weapon]; if (!wep?.ranged) return false;
const d = dist; if d > wep.range) return false;
if (!this.world.lineClear(this.x,this.y,target.x,target.y)) return false;
if (this.cooldown>0) return false;
this.faceTowards(...);
const burst = wep.burst||1;
for i < burst: world.shoot(this,target,{dmg: wep.dmg * (world.hasTech('gunsmithing')?1.2:1)});
this.cooldown = wep.cooldown * (0.95 - this.skills.shooting*0.012) (higher skill faster)
this.attackFlash=0.15;
this.world.play? world.shoot plays.
return true;
```
Rifle burst 3: projectiles all target same; fine.

`tryMelee(target)`.

updateCombatTask:
```js
updateCombatTask(sdt) {
 const w=this.world; const t=this.task;
 let target = t.target ? w.pawnById(t.target.id) : null;
 if (!target && t.targetId) target = w.pawnById(t.targetId);
 if (!target || target.dead) { this.finishTask(); return; }
 t.target = target; t.targetId = target.id;
 if (t.type==='hunt') { if (target.dead) {...} } 
 if (t.type==='attack' && target.downed) { finish; return; }
 if (t.type==='attack' && !w.raid && !this.drafted) { finish; return; }
 const wep = WEAPONS[this.weapon];
 const ranged = !!wep?.ranged;
 const stop = ranged ? Math.min(wep.range*0.9, 9) : 1.2;
 const d = dist;
 if (d <= stop) {
   this.path = []; this.phase='work'; this.working=true; this.faceTowards(target.x,target.y);
   if (ranged) this.tryShoot(target); else this.tryMelee(target);
   this.workAnim += sdt;
 } else {
   this.phase='go'; this.working=false;
   this.repathTimer -= sdt;
   const needsRepath = !this.path.length || this.repathTimer <= 0;
   if (needsRepath) {
     this.repathTimer = 0.65;
     const path = w.pathToTile(this, Math.floor(target.x), Math.floor(target.y));
     if (path) this.path = path; 
   }
   this.moveAlong(sdt);
   // If now within stop distance, no move further; handled next tick.
 }
}
```
Issue: path goes to target tile; when getting close, next frame d <= stop, stops. Good.

If can't path to animal across water, finish. Add path failure counter: if null set repathTimer 1 and maybe finish after 3 attempts. Simple: if null finishTask.

Animals: hunting should stop at range. good.

`updateRaider`:
```js
if (this.downed) return; // handled earlier
if (!this.world.raid) { maybe idle wander }
const target = w.nearestColonist(this.x,this.y);
if (target) {
  const d=dist; wep; 
  if (wep.ranged) {
    if (d <= wep.range*0.92 && LOS) { this.path=[]; face; if cooldown<=0 shoot; }
    else if (d < 30) this.chase(target, sdt);
  } else {
    if (d <= 1.25) { if cooldown<=0 w.melee(this,target); this.path=[]; face; }
    else this.chase(target,sdt);
  }
} else {
  // no targets: attack structures
  if (this.cooldown<=0) {
    const obj = nearest built object within 1.5; if obj damage; else chase colony center
  }
  chase to (30,30)
}
```
`chase(target,sdt)` repath every 0.6s, move. If path null: attack nearest wall adjacent (find object adjacent and damage every 1.2s) - helps raiders breach when target unreachable. Implement:
```js
if (!path) {
  // find object within 1.2 with blocks; melee it
  for o of objects if built && blocks && dist(o center) < 2.2 -> damageObject
}
```
Simpler: path usually exists via doors.

Also raiders wander if no target and no structures.

`updateAnimal`:
```js
this.wanderTimer -= sdt;
const threat = w.nearestRaider(this.x,this.y);
const scared = threat && dist < 6;
if (scared) { flee from threat; } 
else if (this.task) { if phase go moveAlong/arrive; else finish; }
else if (wanderTimer<=0) { pick wander near home; wanderTimer=4+rng*8; beginTask wander; }
```
When fleeing, set task wander to point away with speed maybe; avoid repeated assignment via `fleeCooldown`. Use `this.fleeTimer`: if scared and fleeTimer<=0 → pick point away 5 tiles, beginTask flee, fleeTimer=1.5. Add in updateAnimal. After raid, wander home if far (dist>10) — set wander target near home.

Animals also should not be selected for jobs.

`updateNeeds` for animals can cause starvation; start food 100; not eating. They'd starve over days. Add in updateAnimal: food = 90; rest=90 (skip). Actually updateNeeds decrements. Could set needs to 100 each update for animals. Do at start updateAnimal: this.needs.food = Math.max(40, ...). Not critical in 10 min. But long sessions; add.

Downed animals: `hurt` sets downed below 25%; update() returns before updateAnimal when downed; they never die/recover. Hunters need kill: world.hurt called until dead? Once downed, target.downed true; but hunter task target still animal downed; updateCombatTask doesn't skip downed for hunt, shoots again → hp below 0 → dead. Good. If not finished, animal downed remains. Fine.

Downed raiders: they stop acting; colonists consider target downed → attack task ends. Raid considered repelled when all dead/downed. Fine.

Colonist downed and no doctor: recover after 2 hours; good.

World.nearestColonist ignores downed; raiders then target alive ones, else structures.

Implement `damageStructure` for raiders using world.damageObject with spark.

Medical reservation release if patient dies: release handled by doctor finish only. Fine.

Add `getWeapon` helper.

Also drafted auto-fire uses tryAutoFire:
```js
tryAutoFire() {
 const wep = WEAPONS[this.weapon]; if (!wep?.ranged) return;
 const raider = this.world.nearestRaider(this.x,this.y); if (!raider) return;
 if (dist > wep.range) return;
 this.faceTowards; this.tryShoot(raider);
}
```

`reactToRaid` also handles drafted? drafted pawns are user-controlled; don't auto-chase. Only tryAutoFire.

For undrafted, begin attack if brave; if they have no ranged, melee; else flee.

Raid ended: updateCombat clears; also if drafted and task attack still? Let finish.

One more: `wake()` calls finishTask which drops carry if any; okay.

`this.alarm` starts false. spawnRaid sets alarm and clears tasks. Good.

